    {
      "ts": 1790179513.239694,
      "status": "done",
      "result": {
        "summary": "I read the diff and did not run the tests. The notification and promotion throttling, the shared read-scope helper, and the docs and shadow_n revert match the fix-round rules. One issue remains in decision_log.recent: it still scans the whole log on most ticks. Two low-severity items follow.",
        "verdict": "request_changes",
        "comments": [
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/decision_log.py",
            "line": 263,
            "issue": "Grouped recent() only stops early once every subject has an applied row. In shadow mode, and for any task that has never been steered, no applied row exists. So the scan runs backwards through the entire decisions.jsonl every tick, and the tick cost still grows with total log size, which is the review's complaint. The `limit` argument (limit=2 from steering_tick) is also ignored in grouped mode, so it doesn't bound anything. subjects=[] (no running tasks) also scans the whole file for nothing. Bound the scan, for example by a max rows or bytes window, or keep a per-tick or per-process cache and an early return for empty subjects.",
            "severity": "med"
          },
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/daemon.py",
            "line": 1676,
            "issue": "steering_refusal_reasons is only updated while mode is active. If the config goes active, then shadow or off, then active again with the same refusal reasons, the stale remembered reasons suppress the notification. Reset it when mode is not active.",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/steering_policy.py",
            "line": 33,
            "issue": "safe_scope falls back to Path('.') (the process cwd) when neither a worktree argument nor task['worktree'] is set. Containment is then checked against the daemon's cwd rather than a task worktree. It is harmless in practice, but the fallback is implicit. Return the entries unchanged, or skip the check, when no worktree is known.",
            "severity": "low"
          }
        ],
        "packet_version": "aba47491fa27",
        "confidence": 0.0,
        "provenance": [
          "repo"
        ]
      }
